          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="45450_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Annotating is the third step in the reading process loop, not the final step. The correct order is previewing, questioning, annotating, and reviewing.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g480c0d96887523dbabe5c424ed5c0ed1" title="Question 12">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>70753,49438,24594,68234</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;What is the definition of literacy?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="70753">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The ability to read and write effectively in academic and professional contexts</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="49438">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The ability to memorize large amounts of text quickly</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="24594">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The ability to speak multiple languages fluently</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="68234">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The ability to type written documents without errors</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">70753</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="70753_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">49438</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="49438_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">24594</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="24594_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">68234</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="68234_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">70753</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="70753_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Literacy is the ability to read and write effectively in academic and professional contexts. Modern literacy includes critically evaluating information, understanding complex texts, and communicating clearly across different formats and audiences.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="49438_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Memorizing large amounts of text quickly is not the definition of literacy. Literacy refers to reading and writing effectively, including critical evaluation and clear communication.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="24594_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Speaking multiple languages fluently describes multilingualism, not literacy. Literacy refers specifically to the ability to read and write effectively.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="68234_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Typing written documents without errors describes a technical skill, not literacy. Literacy refers to reading and writing effectively across academic and professional contexts.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g9d17bb4e58a1bfbd00f7729554e1426a" title="Question 13">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1.0</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>57625,45414,22178,74550</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;What does the term &lt;strong&gt;vocabulary&lt;/strong&gt; refer to in academic reading?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="57625">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The range of language and terminology used by an author or academic discipline</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="45414">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The number of pages contained in a textbook</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="22178">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The list of references at the end of an article</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="74550">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">The headings and subheadings found in a chapter</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">57625</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="57625_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">45414</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="45414_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">22178</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="22178_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">74550</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="74550_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">57625</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="57625_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Vocabulary refers to the range of language and terminology used by a particular author, group, or academic discipline. Building vocabulary improves both reading comprehension and writing ability.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="45414_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">The number of pages in a textbook describes the length of a text, not vocabulary. Vocabulary refers to the range of language and terminology used in a text.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="22178_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">The list of references at the end of an article describes a bibliography or reference list, not vocabulary. Vocabulary refers to the range of language and terminology used by an author or discipline.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="74550_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/html">Headings and subheadings are organizational features of a text, not vocabulary. Vocabulary refers to the range of language and terminology used by an author or academic discipline.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
    <item ident="g605a51d767ac209ffc91c5ee295fd38c" title="Question 14">
      <itemmetadata>
        <qtimetadata>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>question_type</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>multiple_choice_question</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>points_possible</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>1</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
          <qtimetadatafield>
            <fieldlabel>original_answer_ids</fieldlabel>
            <fieldentry>47612,71882,72301,46921</fieldentry>
          </qtimetadatafield>
        </qtimetadata>
      </itemmetadata>
      <presentation>
        <material>
          <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;Which reading strategy should you use when you want a general overview of a chapter before deciding if it is relevant to your research?&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
        </material>
        <response_lid ident="response1" rcardinality="Single">
          <render_choice>
            <response_label ident="47612">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Skimming</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="71882">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Scanning</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="72301">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Annotating</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
            <response_label ident="46921">
              <material>
                <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reviewing</mattext>
              </material>
            </response_label>
          </render_choice>
        </response_lid>
      </presentation>
      <resprocessing>
        <outcomes>
          <decvar maxvalue="100" minvalue="0" varname="SCORE" vartype="Decimal"/>
        </outcomes>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">47612</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="47612_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">71882</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="71882_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">72301</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="72301_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="Yes">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">46921</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <displayfeedback feedbacktype="Response" linkrefid="46921_fb"/>
        </respcondition>
        <respcondition continue="No">
          <conditionvar>
            <varequal respident="response1">47612</varequal>
          </conditionvar>
          <setvar action="Set" varname="SCORE">100</setvar>
        </respcondition>
      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="47612_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Skimming is the correct strategy when you want a general overview of a text to determine if it is relevant. You read titles, headings, the first and last paragraphs, and any summaries to quickly assess the content.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="71882_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Scanning is used to find a specific piece of information, such as a name or date. Skimming is the strategy for getting a general overview of a text.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="72301_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Annotating involves marking up a text and adding notes during detailed reading. Skimming is used before detailed reading to get a general sense of the content.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="46921_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reviewing is the final step in the reading process loop and takes place after reading. Skimming is used to quickly assess whether a text is relevant before committing to a full read.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
