      </resprocessing>
      <itemfeedback ident="15893_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Reading the abstract if one is provided is listed as a tip for effective skimming. The abstract gives a concise summary of the text's main ideas, making it a useful tool for quickly assessing content.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="93698_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Moving your eyes in a zigzag pattern across the page is a tip for scanning, not skimming. Skimming focuses on reading titles, headings, and the first and last paragraphs to get a general overview.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="10936_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Using Ctrl+F to search for key terms is a tip for scanning digital texts, not skimming. Skimming focuses on reading titles, headings, and the first and last paragraphs.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="55005_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Writing questions in the margins as you read is part of annotating, the third step in the reading process loop. Skimming is a quick overview strategy used before or instead of detailed reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
