      <itemfeedback ident="26591_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">"What did I learn?" is listed as one of the questions to ask yourself during the reviewing step. This question helps you consolidate and reflect on the content after you have finished reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="27478_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Examining headings and subheadings is part of previewing, the first step in the reading process loop. The reviewing step focuses on reflecting on and consolidating what you learned after reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="26452_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Deciding which annotation symbols to use is part of annotating, the third step in the reading process loop. The reviewing step focuses on reflecting on and consolidating what you learned after reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
      <itemfeedback ident="38820_fb">
        <flow_mat>
          <material>
            <mattext texttype="text/plain">Asking about the author's main point is part of questioning, the second step in the reading process loop. The reviewing step focuses on reflecting on and consolidating what you learned after reading.</mattext>
          </material>
        </flow_mat>
      </itemfeedback>
    </item>
